# Project Statement

## Problem Statement
Spam messages can contain unwanted advertisements, misleading offers, or suspicious requests. Manually identifying every message is inconvenient. SpamShield aims to classify a text message automatically as SPAM or NOT SPAM using NLP and machine learning.

## Scope
The project covers:
- Text message input
- Data loading and validation
- NLP preprocessing
- Machine-learning model training
- Message classification
- Model evaluation
- Prediction report generation

The project is designed as a command-line application and does not send, delete, or modify real messages.

## Target Users
- Students learning AI and NLP
- Developers experimenting with text classification
- Users who want to demonstrate automated spam classification

## High-Level Features
1. Message classification
2. NLP preprocessing
3. Machine-learning model training
4. Model evaluation
5. Prediction report generation
6. Input validation
